   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Write what you want in 'Prompt' and queue.\n\nTo change a picture instead: turn 'Edit an image' on, load the picture in 'Image', and say what to change (e.g. 'make it night', 'give him a red jacket', 'turn this into a watercolor painting'). The result keeps the picture's shape; Width and Height only apply to new images.\n\nTo put a particular face on the person: turn 'Change the face' on and load a clear photo of the face in 'Face photo'. It goes on the main person (the largest face); people in the background keep theirs.\n\n'Negative prompt' lists what to avoid (extra limbs and fingers, deformed faces, a fake look). For paintings, cartoons or 3D, remove those words from it first.\n\n'Model' on Auto picks the best model for the prompt: Z-Image Turbo for realistic people (also several together), Lustify for explicit adult content, Animagine for anime, FLUX.2 Klein for edits and everything else. Choose one there to force it.\n\n'enhance' (on the same node) first rewrites your prompt in detail with a local language model (Qwen3-4B), keeping what you asked for: 'Prompt used' shows the result. Edits keep your exact words.\n\nImages are saved in outputs/comfyui/images, named after the model that made them. Queue again for new variations."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
